title: The Chemnitz Conference
subtitle: The factory councils of Saxony meet to decide on the general strike.
new-page: true
tags: event
view-if: crisis_october = 1 and crisis_time >= 2 and e23_rising_phase = 0 and e23_chemnitz_done = 0
max-visits: 1
priority: 3
on-arrival: {!
if (!RG.e22) { this._runActions(this.game.scenes.e22_lib.onArrival); }
RG.e22.octTick(Q.crisis_time);
RG.e22.leader();
RG.news('Chemnitz: the factory councils of Saxony meet', 2);
Q.e23_chemnitz_done = 1;
Q.e23_ch_p = Math.max(0.05, Math.min(0.95, (Q.e23_oct_hall - 15) / 45));
Q.e23_ch_odds = RG.e22.odds(Q.e23_ch_p);
Q.e23_ch_carried = 0;
Q.e23_hh_rises = 0;
!}

= The Chemnitz Conference

On 21 October, as Reichswehr columns enter Saxony, a conference of factory councils, unions, control committees and the workers' parties meets in Chemnitz. It was meant to give the signal. [+ party_leader +] proposes an immediate general strike in defence of the Saxon government, and everyone who knows the plan knows what the strike is for.

Nobody applauds. Georg Graupe, the Social Democratic labour minister, says that if the proposal is put to the vote his party will walk out. The union delegates look at the floor. Our whips have counted the hall all week, and they call the chances of a vote [+ e23_ch_odds +].

In Hamburg the district leaders are waiting for a courier from this hall. [? if e23_oct_couriers = 2 : They have orders to rise at the first word. ?]

- @vote: Put the general strike to the vote.
- @commission: Hand the proposal to a commission.
- @alone: Rise without the conference.

@vote
subtitle: [? if lock_uprising = 1 : Against the party line: costs Unity. ?] One vote decides it. If the hall says no, the rising is over before it starts.
choose-if: lock_uprising < 2
unavailable-subtitle: The [+ leading_faction_adj +] line forbids a rising.
on-arrival: {!
RG.e22.against('uprising');
Q.e23_ch_carried = Math.random() < Q.e23_ch_p ? 1 : 0;
if (Q.e23_ch_carried) {
    RG.news('General strike in Saxony: the hundreds take the stations', 3);
    RG.ledger('The Chemnitz conference voted for the general strike.', 'e23_chemnitz');
    Q.spd_relation += 4;
    RG.e22.octRise(['saxony', 'thuringia', 'halle', 'berlin'], 'The German Revolution', 'Hold the districts that have risen until the Reichswehr breaks.', 3);
    RG.ecci('trotsky', 6);
} else {
    RG.news('Chemnitz conference votes down the general strike', 3);
    Q.e23_rising_phase = 2;
    Q.e23_hh_rises = Math.random() < [0.6, 0.1, 0.9][Q.e23_oct_couriers] ? 1 : 0;
    if (!Q.e23_hh_rises) { RG.e22.octCallOff(); }
}
!}

[? if e23_ch_carried = 1 : Graupe walks out with a handful of followers. The rest of the Social Democrats stay. The conference votes for the general strike, and that night the hundreds take the stations of Chemnitz, Leipzig and Plauen. ?][? if e23_ch_carried = 0 : The vote is taken by a show of hands, and the hands are against us. The general strike is lost in the hall. That night the Zentrale meets in a Chemnitz flat and calls the rising off. ?][? if e23_ch_carried = 0 and e23_hh_rises = 0 : The order to stand down reaches every district in time. ?][? if e23_ch_carried = 0 and e23_hh_rises = 1 : A courier leaves for Hamburg with the new decision, a day behind the one who left before the vote. ?]

@commission
subtitle: What history did. The party lives to fight again, if the word reaches Hamburg in time.
on-arrival: {!
RG.news('Chemnitz conference refers the general strike to a commission', 3);
RG.ecci('radek', 3);
RG.ecci('trotsky', -8);
Q.e23_rising_phase = 2;
Q.e23_hh_rises = Math.random() < [0.6, 0.1, 0.9][Q.e23_oct_couriers] ? 1 : 0;
if (!Q.e23_hh_rises) { RG.e22.octCallOff(); }
Q.offensive_satisfaction -= 10;
Q.lean_unionist += 2;
!}

The proposal goes to a commission. That night the Zentrale calls the rising off and sends a courier to Hamburg with the new decision. [? if e23_hh_rises = 0 : The order to stand down reaches every district in time, and nothing happens anywhere. ?][? if e23_hh_rises = 1 : Nobody can say whether he will get there before the courier who left earlier. ?]

@alone
subtitle: [? if lock_uprising = 1 : Against the party line: costs Unity. ?] The rising begins, and the Social Democratic workers must choose a side.
choose-if: lock_uprising < 2
unavailable-subtitle: The [+ leading_faction_adj +] line forbids a rising.
on-arrival: {!
RG.e22.against('uprising');
RG.ecci('bukharin', 6);
RG.news('Communists vote the general strike alone: the German revolution begins', 3);
Q.spd_relation -= 10;
RG.e22.octRise(['saxony', 'thuringia', 'berlin'], 'The German Revolution', 'Hold the districts that have risen until the Reichswehr breaks.', (Q.worker_support >= 40 ? 0 : -3));
Q.lean_offensive += 3;
!}

The Social Democrats leave the hall. Our delegates stay and vote the general strike alone, and by midnight the signal has gone to every district.
